  "contract": "Any key used to index, cache, route, or join a piece of state must be a total encoding of that state's identity: it has to include every dimension that can distinguish two logically different entries — the owner/scope that produced the entry, the endpoint/type/path it belongs to, and the runtime type of the value — not merely the payload dimension that some downstream equality check, filter clause, or comparison happens to look at. Two entries that are logically different must never be able to produce the same key; conversely a key must be stable for entries that are genuinely the same. Every file named below either builds such a key, defines the normalization/hash that makes the key total, or consumes the key as an identity for lookup/routing, and so must agree on this completeness rule.",
  "defect_location": {
    "repo": "db",
    "summary": "The live-query 'includes' pipeline runs a correlated subquery per parent entry and then routes each child result back onto the parent row through a routing key. That key is computed by computeRoutingKey() at packages/db/src/query/live/collection-config-builder.ts:1799, which is called from .setupIncludesOutput() (packages/db/src/query/live/collection-config-builder.ts:878), setupNestedPipelines() (packages/db/src/query/live/collection-config-builder.ts:1306), updateRoutingIndex() (packages/db/src/query/live/collection-config-builder.ts:1601-1624) and flushIncludesState() (packages/db/src/query/live/collection-config-builder.ts:1885, 1991). The key it produces is derived only from the correlated value the child computation yields, not from the identity of the parent entry that spawned that computation, so the NestedRouteIndex / NestedRouteReverseIndex / NestedRouteChildToNested structures declared at packages/db/src/query/live/collection-config-builder.ts:1160-1176 cannot separate two parents whose subqueries produce the same value; removeChildKeyFromRoute() (packages/db/src/query/live/collection-config-builder.ts:1560), cleanRoutingIndexOnDelete() (packages/db/src/query/live/collection-config-builder.ts:1741), attachChildCollectionToParent() (packages/db/src/query/live/collection-config-builder.ts:2165) and setIncludedValue() (packages/db/src/query/live/collection-config-builder.ts:2183) then write the child value onto the wrong parent row. The compile-time half of the same key lives in packages/db/src/query/compiler/index.ts, where INCLUDES_ROUTING (packages/db/src/query/compiler/index.ts:64) and getIncludesRoutingKey()/getUniqueIncludesRoutingKey() (packages/db/src/query/compiler/index.ts:1865-1892, called from extractIncludesFromSelect() at :1779, collectIncludesFromSelectValue() at :1845 and compileQuery() at :373) mint the routing namespace the runtime key is written into, so both files must change together. This breaks the contract because the join key encodes only the computed payload and omits the producing parent's identity, exactly the dimension that makes the two cases logically different — the same completeness rule that packages/db-ivm/src/hashing/hash.ts:51-154 (type-tagged hashing, markers at packages/db-ivm/src/hashing/murmur.ts:6-10) and packages/db/src/utils/comparison.ts:187-232 (normalizeValue/normalizeForBTree) enforce for index keys inside this very repository."
